From: le-birnes <226851066+le-birnes@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Copy sparse offscreen presents again even after a present wait.

Premiere's Essential Sound panel (a DXVK swapchain on a child window, copied to the toplevel by 0020)
often kept its previous view after a click: the panel's WM_PAINT rendered and presented the new view,
the copy waited for that present (VK_KHR_present_wait returned) and still picked up the old frame.
Copying again later, with no new present, showed the new view, so the frame was there, just not yet
readable when the wait returned. The delayed second copy now runs for every sparse present, not only
for presents without an id. Ducking test on the hidden screen: 5 of 5 after, about 1 of 3 before.

---
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -2252,8 +2252,10 @@
      * host driver may complete the present asynchronously, so that copy can pick up the
      * previous frame. An app that only presents on change then stays one frame behind for
      * good. When the app tags its presents with present ids (DXVK and vkd3d-proton do),
-     * wait for that present to complete and copy again; otherwise, when presents are
-     * sparse, copy once more after a short wait. */
+     * wait for that present to complete and copy again. When presents are sparse, copy once
+     * more after a short wait in both cases: a completed present wait does not mean the
+     * offscreen window already shows that frame (Premiere's Essential Sound panel kept its
+     * old view after a waited copy, and a later copy with no new present showed the new one). */
     if (res >= VK_SUCCESS)
     {
         static int delay_us = -1;
@@ -2281,7 +2283,7 @@
             }
 
             if (waited || (id && can_wait)) client_surface_present( swapchain->surface->client );
-            if (!waited && now - swapchain->last_present > 25) recopy = TRUE;
+            if (now - swapchain->last_present > 25) recopy = TRUE;
             swapchain->last_present = now;
 
             if (swapchain->paced && is_fifo_mode( app_present_modes && i < ARRAY_SIZE(host_modes) ?
